      <p class="hero-intro">
        The exact position of any element in the periodic table—its Period, Block, and Group—can be easily determined using its atomic number and full SPDF electronic configuration.
      </p>

      <div class="theory-grid">
        <div class="theory-card">
          <div class="theory-card-num">1</div>
          <h3>Electronic Configuration</h3>
          <p>Write the SPDF configuration according to the atomic number using the Aufbau principle.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="theory-card">
          <div class="theory-card-num">2</div>
          <h3>Period Number</h3>
          <p>The highest principal quantum number (n) in the electronic configuration gives the period number.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="theory-card">
          <div class="theory-card-num">3</div>
          <h3>Block Identification</h3>
          <p>The subshell (s, p, d, or f) that receives the last entering electron determines the block.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="theory-card">
          <div class="theory-card-num">4</div>
          <h3>Group Number</h3>
          <p>Calculate the group number using specific rules for s, p, d, and f subshell electrons.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. DETAILED THEORY SECTION -->
    <section>
      <div class="section-title-wrap">
        <span class="section-subtitle">Core Concepts</span>
        <h2>How to Determine Period, Group and Block from Electronic Configuration</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="detailed-theory-grid">

        <!-- s-Block Card -->
        <div class="block-card s-block">
          <div class="block-header">
            <h3 class="block-title">A) s-Block Elements</h3>
            <span class="block-badge">s-Block</span>
          </div>
          <p class="block-desc">
            Elements in which the last electron enters the outermost <strong>s-subshell</strong> belong to the s-block.
          </p>
          <div class="formula-box">
            <div class="formula-title">Group Calculation Formula</div>
            <div class="formula-code">Group = Number of valence s-electrons</div>
          </div>
          <ul class="example-list">
            <li><strong>Sodium (Na, Z=11):</strong> 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s¹ → Last e⁻ in 3s¹ → Period 3, Group 1</li>
            <li><strong>Magnesium (Mg, Z=12):</strong> 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² → Last e⁻ in 3s² → Period 3, Group 2</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- p-Block Card -->
        <div class="block-card p-block">
          <div class="block-header">
            <h3 class="block-title">B) p-Block Elements</h3>
            <span class="block-badge">p-Block</span>
          </div>
          <p class="block-desc">
            Elements in which the last electron enters the outermost <strong>p-subshell</strong> belong to the p-block.
          </p>
          <div class="formula-box">
            <div class="formula-title">Group Calculation Formula</div>
            <div class="formula-code">Group = 12 + Number of p-electrons</div>
          </div>
          <ul class="example-list">
            <li><strong>Chlorine (Cl, Z=17):</strong> [Ne] 3s² 3p⁵ → 12 + 5 = Group 17 (Period 3)</li>
            <li><strong>Neon (Ne, Z=10):</strong> 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ → 12 + 6 = Group 18 (Period 2)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- d-Block Card -->
        <div class="block-card d-block">
          <div class="block-header">
            <h3 class="block-title">C) d-Block Elements</h3>
            <span class="block-badge">d-Block</span>
          </div>
          <p class="block-desc">
            Elements in which the last electron enters the inner <strong>(n-1)d subshell</strong> belong to the d-block.
          </p>
          <div class="formula-box">
            <div class="formula-title">Group Calculation Formula</div>
            <div class="formula-code">Group = Electrons in (n-1)d + ns subshells</div>
          </div>
          <ul class="example-list">
            <li><strong>Iron (Fe, Z=26):</strong> [Ar] 3d⁶ 4s² → 6 + 2 = Group 8 (Period 4)</li>
            <li><strong>Copper (Cu, Z=29):</strong> [Ar] 3d¹⁰ 4s¹ → 10 + 1 = Group 11 (Period 4)</li>
            <li><strong>Zinc (Zn, Z=30):</strong> [Ar] 3d¹⁰ 4s² → 10 + 2 = Group 12 (Period 4)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- f-Block Card -->
        <div class="block-card f-block">
          <div class="block-header">
            <h3 class="block-title">D) f-Block Elements</h3>
            <span class="block-badge">f-Block</span>
          </div>
          <p class="block-desc">
            Elements in which the last electron enters the anti-penultimate <strong>(n-2)f subshell</strong> belong to the f-block (Inner Transition Elements).
          </p>
          <div class="formula-box">
            <div class="formula-title">Group Calculation Rule</div>
            <div class="formula-code">Group = Always Group 3</div>
          </div>
          <ul class="example-list">
            <li><strong>Lanthanides (Z=57 to 71):</strong> Belong to Period 6, Group 3</li>
            <li><strong>Actinides (Z=89 to 103):</strong> Belong to Period 7, Group 3</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

